    strcpy(p, "AAAA");
    /* Do NOT use p after this point */
    p = NULL;               // Prevent accidental reuse
}
```
- Setting `p` to `NULL` guarantees that any stray dereference triggers a segmentation fault rather than undefined behaviour.

### Option 2 – Explicitly Mark as Invalid Without Freeing Again
```c
char *p = malloc(16);
if (p) {
    strcpy(p, "AAAA");
    /* No need to call free again; just avoid further use */
}
/* Optionally set p = NULL; */
```
